---
<p>If you write Rust, you already like most of Bayan's ideas: values by default, no null, errors in the type, exhaustive matching, no garbage collector. Bayan keeps those and trades some power for less to write. You do not write lifetimes in the common case, there are no traits with operators yet, and the types that own memory are fewer. This guide maps Rust to Bayan and then lists what will surprise you.</p>
<p>Every Bayan program on this page was run with the compiler, and the output shown is its real output.</p>

